# Frontend rules (Next.js, React, TypeScript)

## The rule that outranks the others

**No clinical calculation runs in the browser.** No PTA, no air-bone gap, no
questionnaire total, no staging, no drug dose, no severity grade. The server
computes and returns it. Frontend `utils` files may format, sort, pick a symbol
or scale an axis, and nothing else. If you are about to write arithmetic on
clinical values, stop.

## Folder structure

    src/app/          routes only: layout, page composition, data loading
    src/features/     one folder per clinical domain, mirrors the backend
    src/components/   shared, feature-agnostic
      ui/             shadcn primitives (generated, edit sparingly)
      layout/         AppShell, Sidebar, Topbar, PageHeader
      data/           DataTable, EmptyState, FilterBar, Pagination
      forms/          Form, field wrappers, AutosaveIndicator, DirtyGuard
      clinical/       AnatomicalMap, LateralityToggle, ScoreBadge, FindingChip
      charts/         chart wrappers
    src/lib/          api client, i18n, auth, forms, hooks, utils
    src/lib/test/     test automation hooks (test id factory only)
    src/providers/
    src/styles/

Feature folder shape:

    features/<domain>/
      index.ts          public surface. Others import ONLY from here.
      api/              typed HTTP calls + query keys
      hooks/            useQuery / useMutation wrappers
      components/
      schemas/          zod schemas for forms
      types/            view models
      utils/            display only
      constants.ts

- A page file over ~80 lines means logic leaked out of a feature.
- Cross-feature imports go through the barrel. Never
  `@/features/audiology/components/AudiogramChart/symbols`.
- The feature dependency graph stays acyclic.

## Server and client components

- Default to Server Components for read-only first paint (patient header,
  timeline first page, document lists).
- Add `"use client"` only where interactivity requires it, at the smallest
  component that needs it, never at the top of a page.
- Never pass a function, a class instance or a Date across the server/client
  boundary. Serialize explicitly.

## Data fetching and state

- Server state lives in TanStack Query. Never copy it into `useState`.
- Client state (open panel, selected side, active tab) is local state, or a
  small Zustand store per feature when it must be shared. No global store.
- URL state (filters, pagination, selected tab) lives in the URL so a view can
  be bookmarked and survives a refresh.
- Query keys come from the central factory in `lib/api/query-keys.ts`. Never
  write a key literal inline.
- Mutations: optimistic update where safe, invalidate precise keys, roll back
  on error, translated toast.
- Types come from `lib/api/generated/`. Never hand-write an API response type;
  regenerate with `make contracts`.

## Forms

- react-hook-form plus zod plus the shared field components. Never a raw
  `<input>` with manual state.
- The zod schema lives in the feature's `schemas/`. Validation messages are
  translation keys, not sentences.
- Server field errors map back onto inputs automatically through the resolver.
  Do not display a raw server message.
- Clinical forms autosave: debounced PATCH of the dirty subset, IndexedDB draft
  mirror, optimistic concurrency with the record `version`, and a visible state
  (idle / saving / saved / offline / conflict). Never fail silently.
- A 409 opens a conflict panel showing both versions. Never overwrite.

## Internationalization

- Every user-visible string goes through `t()`. An eslint rule blocks literals
  in JSX.
- Keys are semantic and namespaced by feature:
  `audiology.audiogram.actions.addThreshold`.
- Adding a key means adding it to every locale catalog in the same change.
- ICU format for plurals and interpolation. No string concatenation, no
  manual `+ "s"`.
- Dates, numbers and units format through `lib/i18n/format.ts`. Never call
  `toLocaleDateString()` inline.
- Clinical terms render from the concept dictionary by `conceptId`, not from a
  translation key and not from a stored string.
- Layout uses logical CSS properties (`margin-inline-start`, `inset-inline`) so
  RTL needs no mirrored stylesheet.
- Directional icons (back, next, chevron) flip in RTL. Anatomical icons,
  charts, audiograms and anatomical maps do **not** flip. A mirrored audiogram
  is a clinical hazard.
- Never hardcode a unit label; units are constants, not translations.

## Clinical components

- `AnatomicalMap` is data-driven: an SVG plus a JSON region definition with
  `conceptId` and `valueSetId` per region. Adding a map is adding data, not
  React code.
- Audiogram conventions are fixed and not configurable: dB HL descending on Y,
  log frequency on X, red circles right, blue crosses left, brackets for bone
  conduction, arrows for no response.
- Every clinical input supports keyboard entry. Doctors have one hand free
  during procedures. Arrow keys move between frequencies, a key toggles ear,
  a key marks no response.
- Show provenance where a value came from a technician, a device or an accepted
  AI suggestion.

## Accessibility and UX

- Every interactive element is reachable and operable by keyboard, with a
  visible focus ring.
- Labels are real `<label>` elements tied to inputs. Placeholders are not
  labels.
- Every list has explicit loading, empty and error states. No bare spinner over
  the whole page.
- Target contrast AA. This software is used on cheap screens in bright rooms.
- Destructive actions confirm and name what will happen.

## TypeScript

- `strict` is on. No `any`, no non-null assertion (`!`) to silence the compiler,
  no `@ts-ignore` without a comment explaining why and a linked issue.
- Prefer `type` for unions and props, `interface` only when declaration merging
  is genuinely needed.
- Discriminated unions over optional-field soup for variant data.
- Exhaustive `switch` on unions with a `never` default.

## Styling

- Tailwind utilities plus the design tokens in `styles/tokens.css`. No inline
  hex colors, no magic pixel values.
- Compose classes with `cn()`. Do not build class strings by concatenation.
- Print styles live in `styles/print.css`. Clinical screens must print sensibly.

## Visual design

- **Light mode by default.** The product ships in a bright, clinical light theme
  (`forcedTheme="light"`). Dark mode is not a priority for phase 0; do not
  design screens dark-first.
- **Locale switcher.** Every screen exposes `LocaleSwitcher` (top bar when
  logged in; top-end on auth routes). Changing locale updates the URL segment
  and re-renders copy immediately via next-intl.
- **Modern and professional.** Calm medical palette (teal / blue-gray), generous
  whitespace, soft elevation (`tokens.css` shadows), rounded-lg/xl surfaces,
  Inter typography. Avoid cluttered layouts, harsh contrast, or consumer-app
  gimmicks.
- **Clinical context.** Copy and empty states respect that users are clinicians
  in busy practices; auth and shell should feel trustworthy and calm, not
  playful.
- **Consistency.** New screens reuse `Card`, layout shell, and tokens before
  inventing one-off styling. Feature code does not override shadcn primitives
  with bespoke colors.

## Test automation hooks (`data-testid`)

E2E and component tests must not depend on locale, copy, or CSS class names.
Every interactive control and every element tests assert on gets a stable
`data-testid` built only through `lib/test/test-id.ts`.

- **Single factory.** `testId(...segments)` joins dot-separated segments
  (`auth.login.email`). `testIdProps(id)` returns `{ "data-testid": id }`.
  Dynamic ids use typed helpers (`patientRowTestId(publicId)`), never string
  concatenation in JSX.
- **Registry for static ids.** Export a `testIds` object (same idea as query
  keys): nested constants for layout, auth, shared components. Features add a
  namespace (`testIds.patients.list.search`) in the feature or in the central
  registry—never inline literals in components.
- **Coverage.** Buttons, links, inputs, selects, dialogs, toasts, tabs, list
  rows, empty/error/loading states, and page landmarks (shell, sidebar, main).
  Shared wrappers (`TextField`, `DataTable`, `PageHeader`) set the attribute
  once from `name`, `id`, or column id props so features do not repeat it.
- **Locale-safe.** Playwright and RTL tests use `getByTestId` only. Do not use
  `getByRole(..., { name: translatedLabel })`, visible text, or placeholders
  as primary selectors. Role queries are allowed for a11y unit tests, not for
  cross-locale E2E.
- **Stability.** Ids describe purpose, not styling (`submit`, not `blue-button`).
  No auto-generated React ids. Public ids (ULIDs) in dynamic segments are fine
  when the test targets one row or record.

## Testing

- Component tests for anything with clinical input behaviour, especially
  `AnatomicalMap` keyboard navigation and `AudiogramGrid` entry.
- Playwright covers the three killer workflows, run in en, fr and ar to catch
  RTL and truncation breakage; selectors are `data-testid` only (see above).
- Assert user-visible outcomes (text, aria, focus), not React state. Prefer
  `getByTestId` for actions; use `within(...).getByText` only when the assertion
  is explicitly about translated copy, not for finding the control.
